From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] menu: Online Updater leaves out what can't work or would flood the card

On a read-only system image some download folders are on the image itself
(joypad_autoconfig_dir, a video_shader_dir shipped there): those entries
could only fail ("Write failed"; the shaders one silently, as shaders_glsl
can't be made). An entry is left out when its folder, or the nearest existing
one above it, isn't writable (Linux only). The bulk downloads (assets,
cheats, databases, overlays) are left out too: thousands of small files each,
gigabytes on a handheld's exFAT card (cheats: 27924 files, 3.5 GB).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BananaOS-specific]

Rebased by the kiwami fork on RetroArch's master at 71f521e (24 Oct 2026),
from upstream BananaOS's patch for v1.22.2: the same changes, on master's
lines (the entries' labels are MENU_ENUM_LABEL_*_STR there, and the
include block above it has grown).
---
--- a/menu/menu_displaylist.c
+++ b/menu/menu_displaylist.c
@@ -150,6 +150,37 @@
 #endif
 #include "../input/input_remapping.h"
 
+#if defined(__linux__)
+#include <unistd.h>
+/* Online Updater: an entry whose download would go to a folder that can't be
+ * written (a read-only system image) is left out instead of failing. A folder
+ * that doesn't exist yet counts as writable when the nearest one above it
+ * that does is. */
+static bool menu_updater_dir_writable(const char *dir)
+{
+   char path[PATH_MAX_LENGTH];
+   char *slash;
+   if (string_is_empty(dir))
+      return false;
+   strlcpy(path, dir, sizeof(path));
+   for (;;)
+   {
+      if (access(path, F_OK) == 0)
+         return access(path, W_OK) == 0;
+      if (!(slash = strrchr(path, '/')) || slash == path)
+         return false;
+      *slash = '\0';
+   }
+}
+#define MENU_UPDATER_DIR_OK(dir) menu_updater_dir_writable(dir)
+#else
+#define MENU_UPDATER_DIR_OK(dir) true
+#endif
+/* The bulk downloads (assets, cheats, databases, overlays): thousands of small
+ * files each, gigabytes on a handheld's exFAT card (cheats: 27924 files, 3.5 GB)
+ * for things this build doesn't need (RGUI has no assets). Left out. */
+#define MENU_UPDATER_BULK 0
+
 #ifdef HAVE_MICROPHONE
 #include "../audio/microphone_driver.h"
 #endif
